I think you are confused about the function of the &quot;.&quot; dot<br>
character/letter. Its function is *not* to start a sentence.<br>
<br>
The dot {.} is a consonant (pronounced as a glottal stop (or pause)). It<br=
>
precedes words that (would otherwise) begin with a vowel, e.g. {.au},<br>
{.arbaleta}, and also the word {.i}.<br>
<br>
The word {.i} is the sentence separator, not the dot.<br>
